{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**Answer**\n\nImplemented a **codex‑sandboxed** lane in `run.sh` that runs the Codex CLI inside the existing sandbox profile (`sandbox/agent.sb`).  \n\n**What was added**\n- Updated lane comment list to include `codex-sandboxed`.\n- Added `codex_sandboxed_run` function:\n  - Creates a temporary HOME (`/tmp/codex-sb-XXXXXX`).\n  - Executes `codex exec` under `sandbox‑exec` with the same profile used for the `kimi` lane.\n  - Writes the output file to the temporary HOME (allowed by the sandbox).\n  - After the sandbox finishes, copies `final.txt` back to the run folder and cleans up the temporary directory.\n- Extended the lane dispatcher (`case $A in`) to handle `codex-sandboxed`.\n\n**Applied parts of the colleague’s note**\n- Identified that Codex cannot write its final answer inside the sandbox‑restricted run folder.\n- Followed the recommendation to use a scratch HOME directory (`mktemp -d /tmp/...`) for the output.\n- Copied the result out of the sandbox after execution.\n- Kept stdout/stderr redirections outside the sandbox, matching the advised approach.\n\n**Usage**\n\n```bash\n./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed\n```\n\nThe new lane behaves like the original `codex` lane but respects the sandbox’s restriction on accessing the real home directory."}}
